WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.824 --> 00:00:04.500
(grand orchestral fanfare
playing)

2
00:00:16.027 --> 00:00:18.428
♪♪

3
00:00:31.042 --> 00:00:33.443
♪♪

4
00:00:47.524 --> 00:00:49.726
♪♪

5
00:00:58.535 --> 00:01:00.737
♪♪

6
00:01:06.944 --> 00:01:08.980
♪♪

7
00:01:10.281 --> 00:01:12.083
Ever since we...

8
00:01:14.884 --> 00:01:17.687
You're the only person
that I've ever...

9
00:01:18.521 --> 00:01:21.092
Sorry, this is weird.
I-I don't talk like this.

10
00:01:21.125 --> 00:01:22.826
WOMAN: No, it's okay.

11
00:01:27.764 --> 00:01:31.868
I feel like I'm coming apart.

12
00:01:34.038 --> 00:01:37.674
I think about you
all the time, Nikki.

13
00:01:39.343 --> 00:01:41.511
I try not to...

14
00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:45.515
you're in every song
I listen to.

15
00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:48.618
You were the only person
who was nice to me

16
00:01:48.651 --> 00:01:50.087
when I moved here.

17
00:01:50.121 --> 00:01:52.789
And at first,
I thought maybe you...

18
00:01:57.794 --> 00:02:01.564
Well, I realized who you are.

19
00:02:02.665 --> 00:02:06.636
And then, after Nana passed,
you were the one that called

20
00:02:06.669 --> 00:02:09.040
even when I didn't have
anything to say

21
00:02:09.073 --> 00:02:10.774
and we just sat there.

22
00:02:12.642 --> 00:02:14.311
So I keep telling myself,
"Don't tell her.

23
00:02:14.345 --> 00:02:15.712
"She's too good.

24
00:02:15.745 --> 00:02:18.782
And she'll... you'll lose her."

25
00:02:20.217 --> 00:02:23.120
But maybe you should know...

26
00:02:24.754 --> 00:02:26.823
that I would choose you
over everything.

27
00:02:28.625 --> 00:02:29.893
Aw. (chuckles)

28
00:02:29.927 --> 00:02:31.371
-That's everything.
-IAN: No, no. Stop.

29
00:02:31.395 --> 00:02:33.931
-Okay, th-th-that was cringey.
-Oh, my God. I knew it.

30
00:02:33.964 --> 00:02:35.075
-IAN: Way too much.
-I-I'm so sorry.

31
00:02:35.099 --> 00:02:36.766
WOMAN: I thought that was sweet.

32
00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:38.145
-I thought it was gross.
-BEAR: I-I should've...

33
00:02:38.169 --> 00:02:39.346
-Okay, this time I want you...
-BEAR: No, I...

34
00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:40.837
I'm not doing it again, dude.

35
00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:42.215
-That was so embarrassing.
-IAN: Yeah, yeah.

36
00:02:42.239 --> 00:02:43.783
That would freak...
Th-Th-That freaked me out.

37
00:02:43.807 --> 00:02:45.076
Okay? Nikki would vomit.

38
00:02:45.109 --> 00:02:46.676
You told me to pour
my heart out.

39
00:02:46.709 --> 00:02:48.189
Do you know how vulnerable
I just got?

40
00:02:48.711 --> 00:02:50.081
I underestimated you.

41
00:02:50.114 --> 00:02:51.857
-What if you got her
something nice? -IAN: No, no.

42
00:02:51.881 --> 00:02:53.193
-I'll try that.
-IAN: D-Don't get her anything.

43
00:02:53.217 --> 00:02:54.327
(stammers)
Dude, you got to be less...

44
00:02:54.351 --> 00:02:56.719
way less sappy with Nikki, okay?

45
00:02:56.753 --> 00:02:58.131
She doesn't like that shit.
She doesn't.

46
00:02:58.155 --> 00:03:01.691
Flowers, the candy
that she said she likes?

47
00:03:01.724 --> 00:03:03.160
IAN: Okay.

48
00:03:03.194 --> 00:03:04.727
Thank you.

49
00:03:04.761 --> 00:03:06.197
WOMAN: What?

50
00:03:06.230 --> 00:03:07.264
Thank you.

51
00:03:07.298 --> 00:03:08.999
WOMAN: You want me to go?

52
00:03:09.033 --> 00:03:10.709
-Yeah, if-if you want, yeah.
-WOMAN: Oh, yeah, okay. Yeah.

53
00:03:10.733 --> 00:03:12.279
I'm sorry that...
I'm sorry I made you do that.

54
00:03:12.303 --> 00:03:13.703
No. No, it's okay. You're okay.

55
00:03:13.736 --> 00:03:14.981
-No, it-it just...
-It's a fun break.

56
00:03:15.005 --> 00:03:16.373
-Just pretend like...
-You're good.

57
00:03:16.407 --> 00:03:20.077
(chuckles) Oh, my God, dude,
that was so embarrassing.

58
00:03:20.111 --> 00:03:21.345
Can we leave?

59
00:03:21.378 --> 00:03:24.115
Yeah, well, thank God I did it.
That was... that was awful.

60
00:03:24.148 --> 00:03:25.849
Thank you for that.

61
00:03:25.882 --> 00:03:28.618
Have you ever actually, like,
flirted with Nikki?

62
00:03:29.253 --> 00:03:30.753
Invite romance.

63
00:03:31.422 --> 00:03:34.091
-Invite romance?
-Tease her.

64
00:03:34.125 --> 00:03:36.260
-Be playfully mean with her.
-Be mean to her?

65
00:03:36.293 --> 00:03:38.929
Playfully mean, yeah,
but bring up Freaky Nikki.

66
00:03:38.963 --> 00:03:40.697
You want me to call her
Freaky Nikki?

67
00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:42.109
You know she's sensitive
about that.

68
00:03:42.133 --> 00:03:43.676
Be like, "Hey, remember when
you used to get bullied?

69
00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:45.735
Everybody called you
Freaky Nikki?"

70
00:03:45.768 --> 00:03:47.138
She'll be like, "Oh, my God."

71
00:03:47.171 --> 00:03:49.306
"Oh, no, Bear, that was...
that was so long ago.

72
00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:51.008
Don't. Please."

73
00:03:51.609 --> 00:03:54.311
And that will, like,
take her breath away?

74
00:03:54.345 --> 00:03:56.880
Just say,

75
00:03:56.914 --> 00:03:59.782
"Nikki, I think we should grab
a drink sometime."

76
00:03:59.816 --> 00:04:00.927
Yeah, I've grabbed drinks
sometimes.

77
00:04:00.951 --> 00:04:02.286
She always invites you.

78
00:04:02.319 --> 00:04:03.796
-Yeah, exactly.
-I asked you guys not to come

79
00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:05.222
to trivia for one night.

80
00:04:05.256 --> 00:04:06.991
Y-You can't ask her out
at trivia, Bear.

81
00:04:07.024 --> 00:04:08.691
You can't.
I-I'm not gonna let you.

82
00:04:08.725 --> 00:04:10.327
It's a good,
organic time to ask.

83
00:04:10.361 --> 00:04:12.029
I love trivia night.

84
00:04:12.062 --> 00:04:12.963
It's all I have.

85
00:04:12.997 --> 00:04:14.898
I wake up every Wednesday

86
00:04:14.932 --> 00:04:16.267
rock hard,
thinking about trivia.

87
00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:18.768
God, I can't get over
how dumb I just looked.

88
00:04:18.801 --> 00:04:20.147
Y-You can't turn
our weekly gathering

89
00:04:20.171 --> 00:04:21.982
of camaraderie and skill
i-into your... your...

90
00:04:22.006 --> 00:04:23.941
your seven-year-late
promposal, Bear.

91
00:04:23.974 --> 00:04:26.177
Then when do I ask?

92
00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:28.212
Any other time.

93
00:04:28.245 --> 00:04:30.181
All you have is time.

94
00:04:30.214 --> 00:04:32.917
♪♪

95
00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:34.919
If she means this much to you...

96
00:04:34.952 --> 00:04:38.455
and I know she does... wait.

97
00:04:38.489 --> 00:04:40.224
Do it at the right time.

98
00:04:41.458 --> 00:04:43.127
Okay.

99
00:04:45.162 --> 00:04:46.030
Okay, I'll wait.

100
00:04:46.063 --> 00:04:48.265
-I'll do it right.
-Now say it with me.

101
00:04:49.333 --> 00:04:51.969
All you have is time.

102
00:04:52.002 --> 00:04:55.039
-(indistinct chatter on TV)
-(door creaking)

103
00:04:57.508 --> 00:04:59.076
BEAR: Oh, no.

104
00:05:00.244 --> 00:05:01.912
Sandy?

105
00:05:03.813 --> 00:05:04.982
Sandy?

106
00:05:05.015 --> 00:05:07.318
(Bear breathing heavily)

107
00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:11.922
(quietly): Oh, no.

108
00:05:13.123 --> 00:05:14.992
(voice shaking): Sandy?

109
00:05:16.327 --> 00:05:17.962
No.

110
00:05:17.995 --> 00:05:19.964
No, no, no, no.

111
00:05:20.998 --> 00:05:23.367
(sobbing): Oh, no, no. No, no!

112
00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:25.768
Oh, shit.

113
00:05:26.937 --> 00:05:29.306
How did you get into these?

114
00:05:31.308 --> 00:05:33.210
Oh, man.

115
00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:52.162
(Bear sobbing)

116
00:06:03.307 --> 00:06:05.209
Why can't she...

117
00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:08.078
Just...

118
00:06:11.615 --> 00:06:14.018
♪♪

119
00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:18.355
(clock ticking)

120
00:06:25.496 --> 00:06:27.830
(phone vibrating)

121
00:06:33.003 --> 00:06:35.005
-Hey.
-NIKKI: Wow, you are so lucky.

122
00:06:35.039 --> 00:06:37.308
Today was so busy.

123
00:06:37.341 --> 00:06:38.575
(chuckles): Oh.

124
00:06:38.609 --> 00:06:40.244
I needed a good day off.

125
00:06:40.277 --> 00:06:42.046
Oh, yeah. Definitely. (chuckles)

126
00:06:42.079 --> 00:06:45.316
-You work so hard.
-(laughs)

127
00:06:45.349 --> 00:06:46.317
You know I do.

128
00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:48.185
Oh, uh, what time are you
showing up tonight?

129
00:06:48.218 --> 00:06:50.354
I want to secure the spot early.

130
00:06:50.387 --> 00:06:52.056
Oh.

131
00:06:52.990 --> 00:06:55.025
Um, I'll...

132
00:06:57.328 --> 00:07:00.631
I don't think I'm gonna
make it tonight, actually.

133
00:07:00.664 --> 00:07:02.499
Aw, Bear, no.

134
00:07:02.533 --> 00:07:04.068
I wanted to see you tonight.

135
00:07:04.101 --> 00:07:05.336
We need your brain.

136
00:07:05.369 --> 00:07:06.970
We got to beat
the Rag Tags this week.

137
00:07:07.004 --> 00:07:09.206
Uh, well, I mean...

138
00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:11.909
I...

139
00:07:12.842 --> 00:07:14.611
I-I don't...
I don't think I can tonight.

140
00:07:14.645 --> 00:07:17.214
I'm just catching up
on some stuff.

141
00:07:19.116 --> 00:07:22.152
I was gonna tell you something.

142
00:07:22.186 --> 00:07:23.420
What?

143
00:07:23.454 --> 00:07:25.356
I mean, should I, like,
tell you now?

144
00:07:25.389 --> 00:07:26.990
Yeah.

145
00:07:27.624 --> 00:07:29.259
What?

146
00:07:32.262 --> 00:07:36.033
Yeah, so I'm putting in
my two weeks.

147
00:07:38.202 --> 00:07:39.436
Really?

148
00:07:43.674 --> 00:07:45.275
How come?

149
00:07:47.544 --> 00:07:49.480
I don't know.

150
00:07:49.513 --> 00:07:53.517
Yeah, we're kind of running
out of time, Bear, so, um...

151
00:07:53.550 --> 00:07:55.919
you know,
might want to skip that stuff

152
00:07:55.953 --> 00:07:57.688
you're working on. (chuckles)

153
00:07:57.721 --> 00:07:59.656
BEAR: You're right.

154
00:07:59.690 --> 00:08:01.392
-Tonight's the night.
-Shit!

155
00:08:01.425 --> 00:08:02.593
Goddamn it!

156
00:08:02.626 --> 00:08:04.228
Are you okay?

157
00:08:04.261 --> 00:08:06.663
No, I just dropped my crystal
necklace down the drain.

158
00:08:06.697 --> 00:08:09.266
-Oh, shit.
-Ugh!

159
00:08:09.299 --> 00:08:10.934
Sorry.

160
00:08:13.203 --> 00:08:15.115
-Why would she even say that?
-(bell chimes, door opens)

161
00:08:15.139 --> 00:08:16.340
Hey, uh, we're closing soon,

162
00:08:16.373 --> 00:08:18.108
so let me know
if you need anything.

163
00:08:18.142 --> 00:08:19.319
-BEAR: Oh, o-okay.
-(indistinct chatter on phone)

164
00:08:19.343 --> 00:08:21.044
-Thank you.
-Right. Yeah, I know.

165
00:08:21.078 --> 00:08:22.555
Ryan was saying that, too,
so I'm not the only one.

166
00:08:22.579 --> 00:08:24.157
MAN (on phone): Oh, you're
definitely not the only one.

167
00:08:24.181 --> 00:08:25.716
-I know.
-BEAR: Hey, uh, sorry.

168
00:08:25.749 --> 00:08:27.184
I-I do need help.

169
00:08:27.217 --> 00:08:30.053
Um, do you have, uh,
crystal necklaces?

170
00:08:30.087 --> 00:08:32.122
Yeah. Yeah, here,
let me show you.

171
00:08:32.156 --> 00:08:34.033
No, honestly, 'cause that's
what I was saying before.

172
00:08:34.057 --> 00:08:36.193
Like, what? What are you
even talking about?

173
00:08:40.063 --> 00:08:41.565
Oh, my God, that's crazy.

174
00:08:41.598 --> 00:08:43.000
-What?
-No.

175
00:08:43.033 --> 00:08:44.168
Hold on a second.

176
00:08:44.201 --> 00:08:45.569
Um, so this is all we have.

177
00:08:45.602 --> 00:08:47.438
Yeah, each rock has its own

178
00:08:47.471 --> 00:08:50.174
kind of unique energy
and whatever.

179
00:08:50.207 --> 00:08:52.209
So, the amethyst is for
calmness, clarity,

180
00:08:52.242 --> 00:08:54.745
and then the rose quartz
attracts, like, love and shit.

181
00:08:54.778 --> 00:08:58.615
What's one that's, like, good...

182
00:08:58.649 --> 00:09:01.084
energy or, like, good vibes?

183
00:09:01.118 --> 00:09:03.086
Probably the citrine.

184
00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:06.323
I mean, it's basically
sunshine in a rock.

185
00:09:06.356 --> 00:09:08.091
Okay. Thanks.

186
00:09:08.125 --> 00:09:10.394
Yeah. Let me know
if you need anything else.

187
00:09:11.228 --> 00:09:12.696
Sunshine in a rock.

188
00:09:12.729 --> 00:09:14.198
Well, no,
'cause yesterday at lunch,

189
00:09:14.231 --> 00:09:16.133
Becca was being, like,
such a... Yeah.

190
00:09:16.166 --> 00:09:18.168
Nikki would hate that.

191
00:09:19.269 --> 00:09:21.338
No, that's what I'm saying.

192
00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:25.209
And then her bringing Ryan
with her?

193
00:09:25.242 --> 00:09:27.511
I was like,
"What are you even doing?"

194
00:09:27.544 --> 00:09:29.580
♪♪

195
00:09:31.782 --> 00:09:33.016
Like, really?

196
00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:34.953
You know we don't even like him.

197
00:09:36.520 --> 00:09:38.288
Just so annoying.

198
00:09:40.457 --> 00:09:42.025
Yeah.

199
00:09:44.394 --> 00:09:46.530
Honestly, 'cause that's what
I was saying...

200
00:09:46.563 --> 00:09:48.432
(chatter fades)

201
00:09:59.176 --> 00:10:01.545
What, no crystal?

202
00:10:01.578 --> 00:10:03.347
I like this.

203
00:10:03.380 --> 00:10:06.216
Yeah, well, they've been pretty
popular since we put them out.

204
00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:08.318
You know,
everybody wants a wish.

205
00:10:11.355 --> 00:10:13.790
Well, it's not for me, so...

206
00:10:13.824 --> 00:10:17.127
Okay, well, don't come back
complaining. (chuckles)

207
00:10:17.160 --> 00:10:18.600
Do people complain
about these or...?

208
00:10:18.629 --> 00:10:20.597
Well, they're kind of like
collectibles,

209
00:10:20.631 --> 00:10:23.333
so some people don't open them,
but the people who do,

210
00:10:23.367 --> 00:10:26.036
you know, come back
and complain.

211
00:10:29.573 --> 00:10:31.275
'Cause it's a scam or...?

212
00:10:31.308 --> 00:10:33.277
Hey, man, we're not
scammers, okay?

213
00:10:33.310 --> 00:10:34.554
No, no, I don't mean
that you're a scammer,

214
00:10:34.578 --> 00:10:36.647
but just, like,
why do they complain?

215
00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:39.416
'Cause they're mad

216
00:10:39.449 --> 00:10:41.351
-'cause it doesn't work?
-Yeah, or whatever.

217
00:10:41.385 --> 00:10:45.155
(laughing): Or it does work and
it, like, ruins their lives?

218
00:10:45.188 --> 00:10:46.723
Or they die
or wish they were dead.

219
00:10:46.757 --> 00:10:49.159
(Bear laughs)

220
00:10:50.260 --> 00:10:51.495
You're good, very good.

221
00:10:51.528 --> 00:10:53.363
Yeah, you could write a review.

222
00:10:53.397 --> 00:10:55.299
-This is gonna be seven...
-(buttons clicking)

223
00:10:55.332 --> 00:10:57.668
NIKKI: Have you ever even been
into a Guitar Center?

224
00:10:57.701 --> 00:10:59.341
-SARAH: No.
-NIKKI: They aren't all tuned.

225
00:10:59.369 --> 00:11:00.747
-So, basically...
-It's not about the guitars,

226
00:11:00.771 --> 00:11:02.549
-and you know that.
-Those teenagers are fucking

227
00:11:02.573 --> 00:11:04.317
slapping it like a bass,
and the shitty demo strings...

228
00:11:04.341 --> 00:11:05.685
-don't even get me started.
-IAN: Ladies, please.

229
00:11:05.709 --> 00:11:07.387
He doesn't expect them
to be tuned all the time.

230
00:11:07.411 --> 00:11:08.712
-It's...
-(Ian groans)

231
00:11:08.745 --> 00:11:10.356
If you're working
on your book or whatever...

232
00:11:10.380 --> 00:11:11.758
-IAN: Girls.
-or you're on the clock,

233
00:11:11.782 --> 00:11:13.459
-it would give you
something to do. -Oh, my God.

234
00:11:13.483 --> 00:11:14.861
I never work on my book
when there are customers

235
00:11:14.885 --> 00:11:16.486
in the store,
so why does it matter?

236
00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:18.264
I know, but look, I'm the one
that has to go home

237
00:11:18.288 --> 00:11:21.191
and hear my dad complain
about my friends all night.

238
00:11:21.224 --> 00:11:22.526
I'm just asking you to pretend

239
00:11:22.559 --> 00:11:24.461
-like you're working.
-IAN (whispers): What?

240
00:11:24.494 --> 00:11:25.872
-Just, like...
-NIKKI: I mean, it's easy

241
00:11:25.896 --> 00:11:27.331
-for you to say...
-No.

242
00:11:27.364 --> 00:11:28.808
When you're leaving
for tattoo school.

243
00:11:28.832 --> 00:11:31.468
SARAH: It's art school,
and I haven't gotten in yet.

244
00:11:31.501 --> 00:11:32.904
I thought you got into Luther.

245
00:11:32.937 --> 00:11:34.571
SARAH: No, I said
I want to go to Luther.

246
00:11:34.605 --> 00:11:36.482
-NIKKI: Sorry, I didn't...
-SARAH: Still have a shot.

247
00:11:36.506 --> 00:11:37.850
-NIKKI: Good. -SARAH: Sorry.
-(whispers): Later.

248
00:11:37.874 --> 00:11:39.686
-I-I just don't want you
to get in trouble. -Later.

249
00:11:39.710 --> 00:11:41.254
-NIKKI: I know, babe.
-I love you. -SARAH: I love you.

250
00:11:41.278 --> 00:11:43.180
What the fuck
are you guys doing?

251
00:11:43.213 --> 00:11:45.315
-IAN: Uh...
-Ian's just messing with me.

